DNS : Domain Name System
---> DNS translates a human readable domain name into an IP addresss.
eg: www.google.com ----> 198.164.98.27

Route53:
1. Domain Registration
2. DNS management
3. Routing policies
4. Health Checks

TLD: Top Level Domain
--> TLD is the last part of a domain name.
eg: .com, .into
--> Two types of TLD:
1. Generic TLD: gTLD
---> .com , .net, .org, .edu, .gov

2. Contry-code TLD: ccTLD
---> .in, .uk, .us, .cn, .jp


**Steps to Configure Route53:
1. First you have to register domain name. (it can be buy from route53 or any other DNS registrar)
2. Create Hosted Zone on route53.(this is done automatically if the name is resistered using route53)
3. inside hosted zone you will need to create record set.

Hosted Zone:
--> hosted zone is a container for records.
--> Types of Hosted Zone
1. Public HZ:
--> A public hosted zone determines how traffic is routed on the internet.
2. Private HZ:
--> A private hosted zone determines how traffic is routed within an Amazon VPC.


--> for each public HZ that you create, amazon route53 automatically create two records:
1. NS record: (Name Server record)
2. SOA record: (Start Of Authority Record) --> Domain details